README.md
    1→# jq
    3→`jq` is a lightweight and flexible command-line JSON processor akin to `sed`,`awk`,`grep`, and friends for JSON data. It's written in portable C and has zero runtime dependencies, allowing you to easily slice, filter, map, and transform structured data.
    5→## Documentation
    …
    7→- **Official Documentation**: [jqlang.org](https://jqlang.org)
    8→- **Try jq Online**: [play.jqlang.org](https://play.jqlang.org)
    10→## Installation
    …
    12→### Prebuilt Binaries
    …
    14→Download the latest releases from the [GitHub release page](https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases).
    16→### Docker Image
    …
    18→Pull the [jq image](https://github.com/jqlang/jq/pkgs/container/jq) to start quickly with Docker.
    34→### Building from source
    …
    67→## Community & Support
    …
    69→- Questions & Help: [Stack Overflow (jq tag)](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/jq)
    70→- Chat & Community: [Join us on Discord](https://discord.gg/yg6yjNmgAC)
    71→- Wiki & Advanced Topics: [Explore the Wiki](https://github.com/jqlang/jq/wiki)
    73→## License
    …
    75→`jq` is released under the [MIT License](COPYING). `jq`'s documentation is
    76→licensed under the [Creative Commons CC BY 3.0](COPYING).
    77→`jq` uses parts of the open source C library "decNumber", which is distributed
    78→under [ICU License](COPYING)
